  "slug": "graphene-engineering-5eb6",
  "summary": "Five preprints show stacking order, displacement field and Floquet driving tuning valley, Berry curvature and flat-band physics in graphene multilayers and hBN.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that stacking geometry and external fields set the low-energy band structure of layered materials. In ABA trilayer graphene, a displacement field inverts band edges, reverses Berry curvature and splits valleys. In thick rhombohedral graphene, superconductivity is reported with valley-imbalanced Fermi pockets and enhanced by in-plane field. In twisted monolayer-N-layer rhombohedral graphene, narrow topological bands arise from hybridization of Dirac cone and surface states. Floquet driving of twisted bilayer graphene heterostructures yields valley polarization and Chern-number transitions, and shift current in hBN multilayers is proposed as a probe of stacking. The new element relative to strain-focused work is the emphasis on stacking and gating or driving as design and diagnostic handles. The items do not establish one mechanism across systems.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
